{"about_the_game":"<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Commit. Dodge. Strike.</strong><br>In <i>The Elomont Raider</i>, you <strong>move instantly with WASD</strong>, but <strong>once you attack, you can\u2019t move until the action finishes</strong>\u2014and enemies follow the same rule.<br>It\u2019s a classic arcade-style challenge built around timing, openings, and clean execution.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Key Features</strong></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Commit-to-attack combat</strong>: attacking locks movement\u2014choose your moment, then make it count.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Simple controls, real depth</strong>: left click for basic attack, right click for a special skill\u2014each weapon has two forms.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Readable patterns (not full-screen chaos)</strong>: projectiles and AoE threats that reward positioning and patience.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Retro fantasy vibes</strong>: goblins, demons, and diabolical monsters with classic round-bullet visuals.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Nostalgia collectibles</strong>: open chests to find \u201cmemory icons\u201d like game consoles, comics, sneakers, and trophies\u2014small reminders of better days.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Arcade-first pacing</strong>: quick retries, tight stages, and boss fights that test your timing.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Background</strong><br>A modern adult, exhausted by life, is pulled into a strange magical world\u2014one that feels like the fantasies he dreamed of as a kid.<br>Fight forward, recover fragments of memory, and find your way back.</p>","background":"https://store.akamai.steamstatic.com/images/storepagebackground/app/3825690?t=1767424520","background_raw":"https://store.akamai.steamstatic.com/images/storepagebackground/app/3825690?t=176742452